# Q: does the editor's camera take input — the wheel zoom, WASD walk, Q/E turn — or is the
# Q: view the editor opens with the only view there is?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --probe tools/probe/editor-camera.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/editor-camera.txt
#
# The bindings, driven one synthetic frame at a time through the same RtsCamera.Update the
# editor's own update feeds: a probe has no hand on the mouse, so the states are built, and
# what is asked is whether the wiring reaches the camera. The checks are invariants — a key
# held must move the camera — recorded with the numbers measured.
#
#   - `editor wheel <notches> [frames]` rolls the wheel: positive is closer, and the camera
#     eases to it over the frames given.
#   - `editor key <Q|E|W|A|S|D|arrows> [frames]` holds a key: Q/E turn, WASD and the arrows
#     walk the target in the camera's own ground basis.
#
# The failure this pins: the editor's update never fed the camera, so the wheel did nothing
# and the keys did nothing — the screen had exactly one view and no way out of it.

editor key w 30
editor key q 30
editor wheel 6 30
editor wheel -6 30
editor key d 30
editor key a 30
